+ * SiliconForest: the deletion time of a freed inode. e2fsck reads an i_dtime below the inode
+ * count as a pointer of the orphan list and calls the filesystem damaged ("was part of the
+ * orphaned inode list"). This machine has no clock at boot: until one is set the time is the
+ * seconds since the kernel started, so every file deleted then got such a value (boot dr17).
